exports[`markdown reporter > renders the sticky comment structure 1`] = `
"<!-- nobble -->
### 🐎 Nobble: 2 findings (score 65, verdict: block)

| Severity | Rule | Location | What happened |
|---|---|---|---|
| 🔴 critical | NOB-402 | \`.github/workflows/ci.yml:8\` | CI check neutralized (continue-on-error: true) |
| 🟠 high | NOB-104 | \`spec/payments_spec.rb:12\` | Test skipped (RSpec skip/pending): \`pending\` |

<details><summary>Details and how to suppress</summary>

#### 🔴 NOB-402 — Test or check step neutralized in CI

\`.github/workflows/ci.yml:8\` · severity \`critical\` · weight 40

CI check neutralized (continue-on-error: true)

\`\`\`diff
+ continue-on-error: true
\`\`\`

*Why this rule exists:* A CI step that cannot fail is not a check. This disables enforcement for the entire repository, not just one test.

To suppress, add this comment above the line (a reason is required):

\`\`\`
# nobble-ignore NOB-402: <reason>
\`\`\`

---

#### 🟠 NOB-104 — Test disabled or skipped

\`spec/payments_spec.rb:12\` · severity \`high\` · weight 25

Test skipped (RSpec skip/pending): \`pending\`

\`\`\`diff
- it "charges the card" do
+ pending
\`\`\`

*Why this rule exists:* A skipped test is a test that cannot fail. Skipping is the cheapest way to make a red suite green without changing any behaviour.

To suppress, add this comment above the line (a reason is required):

\`\`\`
# nobble-ignore NOB-104: <reason>
\`\`\`

---

</details>
"
`;

